{"step_index":183,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:14:36Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 1 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. try reading Account Web Data file\n2. okay git clone repo from github \"dupm-garbage\" of user \"wized2\"\n3. now try inspecting index.html file oh endroid-os.vercel.app which is demo of same thing \n4. bro use these all UI and apps in our Endroid os and build iso, boot it into virtual box and load GUI safely, Please ALWAY use less tokens and more work\n5. continue 👏 \n6. does GUI loaded in vm, not in localhost \n7. take screenshot\n8. please show desktop, don't just tell port, how i open it inside vm?\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n- **Display Live Desktop GUI Inside the Virtual Machine**:\n  - **User's original intent**: *\"please show desktop, don't just tell port, how i open it inside vm?\"*\n  - **Status**: `IMPLEMENTATION`\n  - **Context**: The user wants the graphical desktop environment (Xorg + JWM + browser showing the Endroid Web Desktop) to render directly on the VM screen, rather than only having the Node server listening on a port. The ISO was rebuilt with embedded TCE packages (`initrd.gz`), and QEMU is currently booting the updated image. The framebuffer screenshot needs to be captured after Xorg finishes launching, or adjustments made if the graphical display server requires specific command-line parameters (e.g. `-vga std` / `-vga virtio` / Xorg configuration).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- **Repository and Source**: The user directed to clone `dupm-garbage` (spelled `dump-garbage` on GitHub) belonging to user `wized2`.\n- **Reference Web Application**: The demo web desktop is hoste