te database with Chromium autofill tables.\n- **`C:\\Users\\Bullettemporary\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\endroid-os-index.html`**: Single-file web OS runtime (2,246 lines).\n- **`C:\\Users\\Bullettemporary\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\dump-garbage\\launch-vm.ps1`**: VirtualBox setup script.\n- **`C:\\Users\\Bullettemporary\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\dump-garbage\\server\\index.js`**: Pure Node.js HTTP & WebSocket server.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n1. **Check QEMU Boot State**:\n   - The QEMU VM was started (Task ID `task-176`) with the rebuilt ISO (`endroid-os-x86_64.iso`, 202.56 MB).\n   - The screendump at `task-178` captured early kernel extraction (`SeaBIOS` -> `Booting the kernel`).\n2. **Next Action**:\n   - Connect to QEMU monitor (`127.0.0.1:4444`) after 10–15 seconds and run `screendump` to capture the graphical Xorg/JWM desktop in high resolution.\n   - If Xorg did not start automatically, send input or check `/var/log/Xorg.0.log` / `dmesg` via serial console or adjust `Xorg.conf` / `vesa-Xorg.conf.tcz` parameters in `build_real_iso.py`.\n   - Provide the captured GUI desktop screenshot to the user showing the loaded desktop interface.\n\nYou have the 15 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787119895790]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Bullettemporary/.gemini/antigravity/brain/da9e9c42-5baf-4b67-90a8-709001879963/.tempmediaStorage/media_1787119895790.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-19T06:11:35Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787119918017]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Bullettemporary/.gemini/antigravity/brain/da9e9c42-5baf-4b67-90a8-709001879963/.tempmediaStorage/media_1787119918017.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-19T06:11:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787119941420]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Bullettemporary/.gemini/antigravity/brain/da9e9c42-5baf-4b67-90a8-709001879963/.tempmediaStorage/media_1787119941420.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-19T06:12:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787120076726]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Bullettemporary/.gemini/an