{"step_index":245,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:23:17Z","content":"The root cause: `tce-load` needs `/etc/sysconfig/tcedir` to point to `/opt/tce` properly. Let me fix the ISO build script directly and reboot with a working one.","thinking":"The issue is clear: `tce-load` can't find the packages because tcedir isn't configured, and `startx` isn't found because Xorg isn't installed. The packages ARE in `/opt/tce/optional/` as .tcz files, but tce-load needs to know where to look.\n\nThe real fix: just directly install the .tcz files using `busybox unsquashfs` or mount them. Actually, the simpler approach is to use `tce-load -i /opt/tce/optional/xorg-server.tcz` with full path - but that's already failing.\n\nWait - looking at the errors: `not found!tcz` - the package name resolution is failing. \n\nThe packages are definitely there with exact filenames like `xorg-server.tcz` and `Xorg-7.7.tcz`, so I could manually extract them using unsquashfs, or just rebuild the ISO with a corrected `bootsync.sh` that auto-loads these packages on boot.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\Bullettemporary\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\dump-garbage\\iso-builder\\build_real_iso.py","EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing ISO build script","toolSummary":"View ISO build script"}}]}
{"step_index":246,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:23:32Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-19T06:23:32Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-19T06:23:32Z\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Bullettemporary/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/dump-garbage/iso-builder/build_real_iso.py`\nTotal Lines: 465\nTotal Bytes: 18591\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n2: \"\"\"\r\n3: Endroid OS — Master Bare-Metal ISO Builder v7 (Complete Graphical Desktop)\r\n4: - Fully self-contained, standalone operating system (zero host dependencies).\r\n5: - Boots into full graphical Xorg + JWM + Dillo desktop automatically.\r\n6: - Bundles 64-bit Linux Node.js runtime and full Endroid Web Desktop server.\r\n7: - Supports UEFI (GPT) and Legacy BIOS (MBR) bare-metal booting.\r\n8: - Auto-mounts persistent data storage (LABEL=ENDROID_DATA) across reboots.\r\n9: \"\"\"\r\n10: \r\n11: import os, sys, shutil, gzip, io, struct, tarfile, zipfile, urllib.request\r\n12: \r\n13: BASE_DIR     = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\r\n14: PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.dirname(BASE_DIR)\r\n15: KERNEL_ASSETS= os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"kernel-assets\")\r\n16: ISOLINUX_BINS= os.path.join(KERNEL_ASSETS, \"isolinux\")\r\n17: TCE_CACHE    = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"tce_cache\")\r\n18: ISO_OUT      = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"endroid-os-x86_64.iso\")\r\n19: STAGING_DIR  = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"iso_staging\")\r\n20: \r\n21: print(\"=\" * 65)\r\n22: print(\"  Endroid OS — Master Bare-Metal OS Builder v7\")\r\n23: print(\"  Target: Physical PC Hardware (Full GUI Desktop, UEFI + BIOS)\")\r\n24: print(\"=\" * 65)\r\n25: \r\n26: # Clean staging area\r\n27: if os.path.exists(STAGING_DIR):\r\n28:     shutil.rmtree(STAGING_DIR)\r\n29: os.makedirs(os.path.join(STAGING_DIR, \"isolinux\"), exist_ok=True)\r\n30: os.makedirs(os.path.join(STAGING_DIR, \"EFI\", \"BOOT\"), exist_ok=True)\r\n31: os.makedirs(os.path.join(STAGING_DIR, \"boot\"), exist_ok=True)\r\n32: os.makedirs(os.path.join(STAGING_DIR, \"cce\", \"optional\"), exist_ok=True)\r\n33: \r\n34: # ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n35: # STEP 1: Extract TinyCore base rootfs\r\n36: # ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n37: print(\"[1/5] Extracting base Linux rootfs...\")\r\n38: base_gz = os.path.join(KERNEL_ASSETS, \"corepure64.gz\")\r\n39: with gzip.open(base_gz, 'rb') as f:\r\n40:     cpio_data = f.read()\r\n41: print(f\"  Base CPIO size: {len(cpio_data)/1024/1024:.2f} MB\")\r\n42: \r\n43: def parse_cpio_newc(data):\r\n44:     \"\"\"Parse newc CPIO archive, preserving all exact header fields.\"\"\"\r\n45:     pos = 0\r\n46:     entries = []\r\n47:     while pos < len(data):\r\n48:         if data[pos:pos+6] != b'070701':\r\n49:             break\r\n50:         header = data[pos:pos+110]\r\n51:         namesize = int(header[94:102], 16)\r\n52:         filesize = int(header[54:62], 16)\r\n53:         name = data[pos+110:pos+110+namesize-1].decode('utf-8', errors='replace')\r\n54:         name_pad = (4 - ((110 + namesize) % 4)) % 4\r\n55:         data_start = pos + 110 + namesize + name_pad\r\n56:         file_data = data[data_start:data_start+filesize]\r\n57:         \r\n58:         mode = int(header[14:22], 16)\r\n59:         uid = int(header[22:30], 16)\r\n60:         gid = int(header[30:38], 16)\r\n61:         nlink = int(header[38:46], 16)\r\n62:         mtime = int(header[46:54], 16)\r\n63:         devmajor = int(header[62:70], 16)\r\n64:         devminor = int(header[70:78], 16)\r\n65:         rdevmajor = int(header[78:86], 16)\r\n66:         rdevminor = int(header[86:94], 16)\r\n67:         \r\n68:         entries.append((name, mode, uid, gid, nlink, mtime, devmajor, devminor, rdevmajor, rdevminor, file_data))\r\n69:         if name == 'TRAILER!!!':\r\n70:             break\r\n71:         data_pad = (4 - (filesize % 4)) % 4\r\n72:         pos = data_start + filesize + data_pad\r\n73:     return entries\r\n74: \r\n75: _ino_counter = [1000000]\r\n76: \r\n77: def make_cpio_entry(name, data=b'', mode=0o100755, uid=0, gid=0, nlink=1, mtime=0, devmajor=3, devminor=1, rdevmajor=0, rdevminor=0):\r\n78:     name_bytes = name.encode('utf-8') + b'\\x00'\r\n79:     namesize = len(name_bytes)\r\n80:     filesize = len(data)\r\n81:     if name == 'TRAILER!!!':\r\n82:         ino = 0\r\n83:     else:\r\n84:         _ino_counter[0] += 1\r\n85:         ino = _ino_counter[0]\r\n86:     header = (\r\n87:         b'070701'\r\n88:         + f'{ino:08X}'.encode()\r\n89:         + f'{mode:08X}'.encode()\r\n90:         + f'{uid:08X}'.encode()\r\n91:         + f'{gid:08X}'.encode()\r\n92:         + f'{nlink:08X}'.encode()\r\n93:         + f'{mtime:08X}'.encode()\r\n94:         + f'{filesize:08X}'.encode()\r\n95:         + f'{devmajor:08X}'.encode()\r\n96:         + f'{devminor:08X}'.encode()\r\n97:         + f'{rdevmajor:08X}'.encode()\r\n98:         + f'{rdevminor:08X}'.encode()\r\n99:         + f'{namesize:08X}'.encode()\r\n100:         + b'00000000'\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
